 "result": "I documented 12 repos this run. All 12 were new backfills, so each got a README, a CHANGELOG and release jobs in `publish.json`. They are the day-named repos from 2026-11-25 and 2026-11-26: ten-turn-machine, turret-sight, lobhill, hopper, starfighter, bingo and its server, casino and its server, ghostwing, centipede and rocketbench.\n\nEvery docs push and the profile push went through, and I made no `vercel.json` change. None of those repos has app files in a subfolder that the root deploy would miss.\n\nBackfills left: none. The repos that still need work are all ones with new commits, not backfills. They are field-twin, hubview, mohavetech-website, itchy-troll, the testbed, blue-agent, downfree-foundry, scores, shared-server and a few Android and backend repos. The 12-repo cap was reached, so they wait for the next run. Most of the other newer `pushedAt` values were bulk bot touches, not real commits.\n\nI reached every repo I tried. I did not touch `sudosilo`, `control-troll` or `heckle-troll`, which are skipped on purpose.\n\nThe profile in `sudosilo/sudosilo` is rebuilt and pushed. The state files, the new notes and `publish.json` are committed to control-troll main as \"scribe state\". The 12 releases and repo settings will be created when the `scribe-publish` workflow runs; I did not check that it has run.\n\nThe Ghost Wing repo's only page is a copy of Tile-topia, so I described it as a tile game under the Ghost Wing name. `agents/notes/general.md` is now well over 40 lines, and I added to it without condensing it.",
